Hub pre-release smoke 2026-11-10 (main, perl 5.14.4, requires only) and CPAN Testers for 0.005 (5.18.4, 5.30.3, 5.32.1 red; 5.36.0 green apart from old YAML modules). The cpanfile says perl 5.014. Classes:
1. lib/File/SOPS/Encrypted.pm _has_public_pv (around 2024, guard 1020-1047): assumes stringifying an NV sets only the private POK. True from 5.36 on; before, the public flag is set and +Inf/NaN "states a string half" (t/39:310, t/46:176/221, t/52:382, t/54:347ff). Code defect for < 5.36, not repairable by a test gate alone.
2. No Perl_strtod before 5.22: Cpanel::JSON::XS reads 0.3 as 0.30000000000000004 (t/23:140/190, t/87:53; Format/JSON.pm 72, 118, 645) and perl reads 5e-324 as 0 and DBL_MAX as Inf (t/39:173; Format/YAML.pm 795-819).
3. Regex: a{,3} is fatal on 5.30-5.32 and a literal before (t/62:243-248); /i folding of \x{e4} and of sharp s is broken on 5.14 (t/62:104, t/77:43; Metadata.pm 1619, 1665).
4. Tests only: t/24:11 imports POSIX signbit (5.22+); t/32:53/83 names the warnings category experimental::builtin (5.36+).
Two ways: (A) the dist requires perl 5.036 and all four classes are gone; (B) the dist keeps older perls: 1 needs another way to tell a number from a string, 2 needs an own decimal conversion below 5.22, 3 a rewrite of {,n} and a floor of 5.16 or 5.18, 4 test gates. Needs the maintainer: which floor.

2026-11-10 19:37 MAINTAINER DECISION (Getty, 2026-11-10): the floor is perl 5.022. Classes 1, 3 and 4 are built for 5.22 to 5.34; class 2 (no Perl_strtod) and the 5.14 regex folding fall away with the floor.

